# --- office and editor junk ------------------------------------------------------------------
# LibreOffice writes one of these beside every open spreadsheet. One of them got committed.
.~lock.*#

# --- artifacts/ ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# One rule, replacing a page of them: nothing under artifacts/ is tracked except the backup.
#
# core/paths.py always stated the policy -- "pushable source lives at the project root;
# everything we can't push (copyrighted data + generated output) lives under artifacts/,
# git-ignored" -- and the tree did not obey it. 118 MB was tracked, 64 MB of it converted
# publisher full text across 1,027 files, which is not ours to redistribute. The rest was
# output: review and adjudication HTML, release workbooks, the macro file, the figures.
#
# artifacts/backup/ is the exception and is built by tools/backup.py, not by hand: the LLM runs'
# extractions and verdicts, the curated answer key, the chemists' decisions, the Scopus funnel
# and the Gao CSVs. 43 MB, and none of it can be recomputed from what is pushed. Everything
# else under artifacts/ either can be, or must not leave this machine.
#
# `backup.py --check` fails if that folder has gone stale or is missing a declared input, so
# "the repository is enough to rebuild the paper" is tested rather than asserted.
#
# No trailing comments on the patterns. gitignore only treats "#" as a comment at the start of
# a line, so "pattern  # why" is a pattern containing spaces and a hash, and matches nothing --
# which is exactly how the first version of this section silently ignored none of it.
/artifacts/*
!/artifacts/backup/

# PDFs are output, or someone else's paper. The manuscript's own figures were excepted here so
# that latexmk on a fresh checkout would not fail at the first \includegraphics; they are not
# any more, because they are generated -- restore the backup and run scripts/paper.sh, which
# draws them from the checks.
*.pdf
